    {
      "id": "TENB-2",
      "name": "groove-repair helix for K78E / R132E",
      "class": "designed protein (from scratch)",
      "concept": "The inverse use, and the one nobody has proposed. Instead of blocking the patch, hold it: K78E and R132E are recruitment-loss alleles whose defect is a single missing positive charge, and the charge-swap rescue (E215K) is established. This helix does not span - it sits in the groove, with acids at i and i+3 (5.05 A) matching the measured K78-R132 separation of 4.35 A and a hydrophobic face against the TEN 129-132 loop. It supplies in trans what the mutation removed, and it is the exact complement of TELM-1.",
