  "novelty": [
    {
      "found": "no small molecule against the TEL patch",
      "detail": "Nandakumar 2012 proposed the patch as 'a new target for anticancer drug development'; Sekne 2022 restated it as 'a rational basis for drug design'; Lim 2023 (Commun Chem) stated 'we have recently discovered the first TPP1 ligands with anticancer activity whose pharmacological characterization is underway'. No structure, series or affinity was ever published. BIBR1532 is a TERT/TER pseudoknot-site inhibitor, not a patch ligand.",
      "verdict": "genuine gap, still open as of this search"
    },
    {
      "found": "TPP1-OB expressed as a dominant-negative",
      "detail": "Yang 2019 (J Cancer Res Clin Oncol) overexpressed the TPP1 OB domain to sequester telomerase. That is the whole protein, not a designed mimetic, and it is not a molecule.",
      "verdict": "precedent for the mechanism, not for the design"
    },
    {
      "found": "de novo binders exist for other targets, none for telomerase",
      "detail": "RFdiffusion, BindCraft and AlphaProteo reach 10-88 % experimental success on their benchmark targets. None has been applied to TERT or TPP1 in the published record.",
      "verdict": "method is available; the target is untouched"
    },
    {
      "found": "allosteric-network analysis of TPP1 proposes exactly these ligands",
      "detail": "Lim 2023 (Commun Chem 6:230) closes by proposing 'allosteric enhancers of the TPP1-TERT binding interaction ... to contrast telomeropathies' and 'allosteric inhibitors ... as a novel class of anticancer agents'. They name the idea and stop at the proposal. TENB-2 is that enhancer made concrete.",
      "verdict": "the concept is on record; no molecule was designed from it"
    }
  ],
